nd explain precisely what true and false mean. Never relabel a licensing trigger as compliance, prohibition or licence possession. For non-Boolean results use [VALUE] and state the units. These meanings are proposals, not approvals.","method":"Parse each actor, trigger, duty, permission, prohibition and exception; then check cross-references and effective dates.","move":null,"parent":null,"protocol":"legalmath.search.v1","role":"normative","source_packet":{"authority":"RETAINED_SOURCE","dependencies":[{"dependency_id":"missing.4ad6b317ad4ade41b82f120a","source_hash":null}],"family_ids":["scope","definitions","exceptions","modality","time","dependencies"],"selected_slice":"Mandatory e-IP route for applications/submissions administered by IPD, with the extended 30 November 2024 cutover.","source_key":"assurance.3fb3cb241815dcbd7d3d754b","units":[{"locator":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u0.0","normative":true,"span":null,"text":"This circular informs the industry that the Securities and Futures Commission (SFC) will extend the parallel run period of its new online application/submission system for investment products, e-IP, by one month to 29 November 2024. After the extended period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by the Investment Products Division (IPD)1 must be submitted to IPD via e-IP from 30 November 2024.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u0.0"},{"locator":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u1.427","normative":true,"span":null,"text":"Background","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u1.427"},{"locator":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u2.439","normative":true,"span":null,"text":"Following the “Circular on launch of e-IP application/submission system on WINGS” dated 8 July 2024, the SFC launched e-IP on its WINGS2 portal on 29 July 2024 to streamline and enhance the efficiency of processing new product applications and post-authorisation/registration submissions to IPD.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u2.439"},{"locator":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u3.737","normative":true,"span":null,"text":"A three-month period of parallel run from the launch of e-IP up to 29 October 2024 was provided at the initial stage. During this period, the SFC continues to accept applications and submissions via existing channels.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u3.737"},{"locator":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u4.956","normative":true,"span":null,"text":"Parallel run period extension and upcoming enhancements","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u4.956"},{"locator":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u5.1013","normative":true,"span":null,"text":"Since its implementation, the SFC has closely monitored the functioning of e-IP and actively engaged with industry participants to obtain their feedback on user experience.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u5.1013"},{"locator":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u6.1187","normative":true,"span":null,"text":"While e-IP has garnered widespread industry support and is running smoothly, new features and more advanced settings will be introduced to further enhance user experience based on users’ comments. To facilitate these enhancements, the SFC will extend the parallel run period of e-IP by one month to 29 November 2024.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u6.1187"},{"locator":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u7.1505","normative":true,"span":null,"text":"Full adoption of e-IP","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u7.1505"},{"locator":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528","normative":true,"span":null,"text":"Starting 30 November 2024, ie, after the parallel run period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by IPD must be submitted via e-IP. The current submission requests from IPD via the IP E-submission system will be integrated into e-IP, including reporting of net asset values, large redemptions and suspensions of dealing. In addition, e-IP users can also settle recurring annual fees associated with relevant investment products through the new system.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528"},{"locator":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u9.2011","normative":true,"span":null,"text":"Feedback and enquiries","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u9.2011"},{"locator":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u10.2035","normative":true,"span":null,"text":"The SFC will continue to review and enhance the operation of e-IP where practicable. If you have any questions, please contact the relevant case officers.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u10.2035"},{"locator":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u11.2191","normative":true,"span":null,"text":"Investment Products Division","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u11.2191"},{"locator":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u12.2220","normative":true,"span":null,"text":"Securities and Futures Commission","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u12.2220"},{"locator":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u13.2256","normative":true,"span":null,"text":"End","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u13.2256"},{"locator":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u16.2270","normative":true,"span":null,"text":"1 Investment-linked assurance schemes, mandatory provident fund products, open-ended fund companies, paper gold schemes, pooled retirement funds, real estate investment trusts, unit trusts and mutual funds and unlisted structured investment products.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u16.2270"},{"locator":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u17.2522","normative":true,"span":null,"text":"2 Web-based INteGrated Service.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u17.2522"}]},"task":"GENERATE"},"configuration":"ignore-user-config; read-only; tools-disabled; no-resume","events_jsonl":"{\"type\":\"thread.started\",\"thread_id\":\"01a0d851-3f74-7b51-ab80-4d9b32ea1951\"}\n{\"type\":\"turn.started\"}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_0\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"{\\n  \\\"coverage\\\": [\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"States the extended parallel run and mandatory route from 30 November 2024.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d19f9ecf9fd26.u0.0\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Background heading.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d19f9ecf9fd26.u1.427\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Identifies launch, portal, submission categories and an earlier circular whose contents are unavailable.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d19f9ecf9fd26.u2.439\\\"},\\n    {\\\"