e these enhancements, the SFC will extend the parallel run period of e-IP by one month to 29 November 2024.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u6.1187"},{"quote":"The current submission requests from IPD via the IP E-submission system will be integrated into e-IP, including reporting of net asset values, large redemptions and suspensions of dealing.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528"},{"quote":"In addition, e-IP users can also settle recurring annual fees associated with relevant investment products through the new system.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528"},{"quote":"1 Investment-linked assurance schemes, mandatory provident fund products, open-ended fund companies, paper gold schemes, pooled retirement funds, real estate investment trusts, unit trusts and mutual funds and unlisted structured investment products.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u16.2270"}],"distinction":"Submission-event routing is the strongest supported reading: the text covers applications and submissions without limiting the mandate to newly opened cases. A new-cases-only alternative would materially spare later filings in existing cases, but the supplied text does not support that exception sufficiently to formalize it as a competing reading. The strongest uncertainty is transitional treatment in unavailable referenced material.","family":"scope","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"Whether the selected event is an application or submission to IPD concerning an investment product administered by IPD, interpreted with the listed product categories. Classification of borderline events requires judgment.","name":"is_covered_submission","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d19f9ecf9fd26.u0.0","d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528","d19f9ecf9fd26.u16.2270"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"Gregorian date of the selected submission event. Selecting the operative event for attempted, incomplete or continued filings may require judgment.","name":"submission_date","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d19f9ecf9fd26.u0.0","d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528"],"type":"date","unit":"Gregorian calendar date"},{"meaning":"Whether the selected application or submission was submitted to IPD through e-IP.","name":"submitted_via_e_ip","requires_judgment":false,"source_unit_ids":["d19f9ecf9fd26.u0.0","d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"}],"result":"submitted_via_e_ip","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and is_covered_submission (>= submission_date (date 2024-11-30)))"},"local_id":"reading_1","questions":["Does the earlier circular provide a transitional rule for pending cases or an exception for particular submission types?","Which operational event fixes the date when a filing spans the cutover?"],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_COMPLIANT] For a covered submission dated on or after 30 November 2024, true means the selected mandatory e-IP routing control is met because that submission used e-IP; false means that routing control is unmet. Outside the stated scope, this result makes no compliance determination. Unknown coverage, dates or channel facts remain unknown.","subject":"Mandatory e-IP routing for one IPD application or submission"}]},"run_id":"run.b85c4487afc44cd9861eb3f43d494627"}